### 7. Marketplace business logic

Implement these business rules on the backend.

#### Multi-seller orders

A customer must be able to purchase products from multiple sellers in one checkout.

Create one customer-facing order and separate seller fulfillment groups.

Each seller must see only their own order items and permitted customer delivery information.

#### Product pricing

Calculate:

- MRP.
- Selling price.
- Discount.
- Coupon discount.
- Tax.
- Shipping.
- Final payable amount.

Use integer minor currency units. Never use floating-point calculations for money.

#### Commission

Support configurable commission by:

- Global marketplace rate.
- Product category.
- Seller.
- Specific product.

Record the commission at order-item level so historical orders are not changed when rates are updated.

#### Inventory

Reserve stock during checkout using an atomic transaction and a configurable reservation expiry.

Prevent overselling and release reservations after failed or expired payments.

#### Payments

Support payment initiation, gateway verification, webhook processing, refunds and reconciliation.

Make payment webhook handling idempotent.

#### Seller settlements

Calculate seller payable amounts using captured payments, commission, refunds and approved deductions.

Maintain an immutable ledger and settlement history.

Do not release settlement until the configured delivery, return and dispute rules are satisfied.

#### Returns and refunds

Support partial returns and partial refunds at order-item level.

Use configurable return windows and product-category return policies.

Record every status change.

